  rx("Migraine — acute attack", "Triptan (with the analgesic)", "Migraine not relieved by simple analgesia", "Adults", "Sumatriptan", "50–100 mg (25 mg also available)", "Oral", "Second dose after at least 2 hours if needed", "Max 200 mg in 24 hours", "Not recommended under 18 years (label 8.4); NICE prefers a nasal triptan at 12–17 years.", NOT_ABX, NS, "Mild to moderate impairment: max single dose 50 mg; severe impairment: contraindicated (label 2.2).", ["Attacks treated per month (more than 4 in 30 days not established, label)"], ["Ischaemic heart disease, uncontrolled hypertension, stroke or transient ischaemic attack (TIA), hemiplegic or basilar migraine, ergot within 24 hours, monoamine oxidase-A (MAO-A) inhibitor within 2 weeks (label 4)"], "suma", "sections 2.1–2.2, 4"),
